      "data": {
        "text": "**Considering Secret Management**\n\nOkay, I'm leaning towards AWS Secrets Manager as the concrete external provider. The key is now to make the provider easily identifiable within the Python script, so the file can be executed correctly. My next step will be to examine the various libraries to connect to AWS Secrets Manager.\n\n\n**Defining AWS Integration**\n\nI've decided to proceed with AWS Secrets Manager, making AWS the identifiable external provider. I'm focusing on using the `boto3` library, now to connect to the AWS secret. I've formulated a solid plan: Create the Python file, import `boto3`, define a placeholder for the secret name, and use the `write` tool to put it all together.\n\n\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789820769555,
          "start": 1789820766183
        },
        "type": "reasoning"
      },
      "id": "prt_0b9a187e7001vA08riGAC16sk1",
